					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yamiaainferno" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3083335); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3083335&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606920842" alt="yamiaainferno" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3083335)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yamiaainferno" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3083335); return false;" >yamiaainferno</a></span> <span class="odate time_1493616274 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 May 2017 05:24</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2806850">
									

<p>An enjoyable read! Novel, mysterious, some good body horror in there. I have a couple of suggestions for improvements, however:</p>
<ul>
<li>The number of notes seems excessive. A lot of them could be part of the proper text of the entry, and others are simply redundant.</li>
<li>The foundation really seemed to be slack with this one. Things were clearly getting out of hand, and yet they seem to have taken no action until the end. As soon as the tenrec's intelligence started to significantly jump, I feel like they would have been worried. By the time it was approaching near-human levels, they <em>definitely</em> would have been worried.</li>
<li>I was disappointed with the lack of content about SCP-3233 herself. No interviews with her, no mention of anyone ever asking her about the containment breach, when she began to exhibit anomalous properties, what her theories were, how she relates to the tenrecs, or about what is causing her anxiety/depression. It seems odd to me that they wouldn't ask these things.</li>
</ul>

							</div>

								
					
